{"id":"b7","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":10,"of":17,"title":"Two nouns, one idea","titleHe":"סְמִיכוּת","goal":"Read and build construct chains — Hebrew's compound noun.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"To join two nouns, Hebrew puts them side by side. The first one carries the meaning of of and often changes shape to do it: בַּיִת house plus סֵפֶר book gives בֵּית סֵפֶר, a school."},{"type":"table","caption":"The first noun shortens","head":["alone","in a chain"],"rows":[["בַּיִת — house","בֵּית סֵפֶר — school"],["בַּיִת — house","בֵּית חוֹלִים — hospital"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה — family","מִשְׁפַּחַת כֹּהֵן — the Cohen family"],["עוּגָה — cake","עוּגַת שׁוֹקוֹלָד — chocolate cake"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"The article goes on the second word, never the first: בֵּית הַסֵּפֶר is the school. Writing הַבֵּית סֵפֶר is the classic mistake."},{"type":"tip","body":"In the plural it's the first noun that pluralises, because it's the one being counted: בָּתֵּי סֵפֶר, schools."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בֵּית סֵפֶר","en":"school","translit":"beit sefer"},{"he":"בֵּית חוֹלִים","en":"hospital","translit":"beit cholim"},{"he":"בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","en":"synagogue","translit":"beit knesset"},{"he":"עוֹרֵךְ דִּין","en":"lawyer","translit":"orech din"},{"he":"כַּדּוּרֶגֶל","en":"football","translit":"kaduregel"},{"he":"יוֹם הֻלֶּדֶת","en":"birthday","translit":"yom huledet"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["school","no, not","narrow","brother"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֵּית סֵפֶר","translit":"beit sefer"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hospital","proof","science","writing"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֵּית חוֹלִים","translit":"beit cholim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["synagogue","certificate","darkness","stops"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","translit":"beit knesset"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["lawyer","pupil","happy","Passover"],"correct":0,"prompt":"עוֹרֵךְ דִּין","translit":"orech din"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["football","see there (עי״ש)","spring","leaf"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כַּדּוּרֶגֶל","translit":"kaduregel"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["Hanukkah","dust","birthday","wing (construct)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"יוֹם הֻלֶּדֶת","translit":"yom huledet"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בֵּית סֵפֶר","school"],["בֵּית חוֹלִים","hospital"],["בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","synagogue"],["עוֹרֵךְ דִּין","lawyer"],["כַּדּוּרֶגֶל","football"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “school”?","options":["טוֹב","בֵּית סֵפֶר","אוּלַי","רָגִיל"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","בֵּית חוֹלִים","עוֹרֵךְ דִּין","יוֹם הֻלֶּדֶת"],"correct":2,"say":"עוֹרֵךְ דִּין","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“The school” is —","options":["בֵּית הַסֵּפֶר","הַבֵּית סֵפֶר","הַבֵּית הַסֵּפֶר","בֵּית סֵפֶר הַ"],"correct":0,"why":"In a construct chain the article attaches to the second noun only."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “synagogue”?","options":["בְּ","תַּנָּא","גְּלִידָה","בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “hospital”?","options":["סְלִיחָה","בֵּית חוֹלִים","לָלֶכֶת","מִצַּד אֶחָד"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"יוֹם הֻלֶּדֶת","translit":"yom huledet","en":"birthday"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “football”?","options":["מַחֲשָׁבָה","אָבִיב","נֶפֶשׁ","כַּדּוּרֶגֶל"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “synagogue” in Hebrew","answer":"בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","hint":"beit knesset"}]}